            url: "/admin/2fa",
            type: "POST",
            data: {
                code: 1234,  // <-- HARDCODED OTP!
            },
            ...


```

The OTP is hardcoded as `1234` in the JavaScript instead of using the user-entered value, so I can bypass the 2FA by sending a POST request to `/admin/2fa` with `code=1234`.

